# Methodex build context exclusions (shared by Dockerfile.web and Dockerfile.mcp).
#
# The Dockerfiles COPY only named subtrees today, so nothing below would reach an
# image anyway — but that is an accident of the current COPY lines, not a
# guarantee. One `COPY . /app` and any of these would ship. Keep the guard
# structural.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.bak-*
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yml.bak-*

# Deploy-root documents that describe the build environment rather than the
# service. They are not part of this repository, but the rule keeps them out of
# the image if a deploy tree is ever used as the build context.
DPR.md
RECONCILIATION_*.md
_mcp_probe.py

# `COPY Technical/campaign/state` must carry only the four corpus files the
# service actually reads (methodology_documents.json, revision_events.json,
# statistics.json, measures.json) — never the build scripts or the campaign
# state that sit beside them in a working tree.
Technical/campaign/state/**/*.py
Technical/campaign/state/campaign_state.json
